WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.888
KIRINOSHIMA JUNIOR HIGH SCHOOL

00:13.972 --> 00:16.558
That club sucked the life out of me.
I couldn't wait to finally be

00:16.641 --> 00:17.934
done with it.

00:18.018 --> 00:20.895
Uh, can we talk about Miki for a sec?
Like, she was always way too into it,

00:20.979 --> 00:22.022
wasn't she?

00:22.105 --> 00:25.316
- Totally.
- I never said anything, but she was a lot.

00:25.400 --> 00:26.526
I know, right?

00:26.609 --> 00:27.736
It's like "calm down."

00:28.403 --> 00:29.863
I had to get out of there...

00:29.946 --> 00:31.948
Become someone new, somewhere else.

00:33.658 --> 00:37.579
So I started going to a cram school in a
different city so I could escape, and

00:37.662 --> 00:41.541
INCREASE YOUR CHANCES FOR PASSING!
ACCEPTING STUDENTS FOR THE NEW SCHOOL YEAR

00:43.585 --> 00:45.545
I knew the transition wouldn't be easy...

00:46.212 --> 00:48.381
But I haven't made a single friend yet.

00:48.465 --> 00:50.967
They've already formed their own little
cliques.

00:51.760 --> 00:53.094
Should I talk to them?

00:53.178 --> 00:55.555
- No, that's way too scary.
- GROUP GIRLS

00:55.638 --> 00:58.558
I mean, let's say I become friends with
them. Seems like girls pretend to be

00:58.641 --> 01:01.102
friendly to your face, then turn
around and talk about you behind

01:01.186 --> 01:02.437
your back.

01:03.730 --> 01:05.857
- Ugh! Even the thought of it is
- UGH...

01:05.940 --> 01:08.193
traumatizing me all over again.

01:16.159 --> 01:17.285
I'm so alone.

01:19.662 --> 01:20.497
Hi, there.

01:21.039 --> 01:22.874
Can I... sit with you?

01:28.213 --> 01:29.047
Who're you?

01:29.130 --> 01:32.342
Huh? Oh! My name is Minato Amamiya.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.680
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

03:09.063 --> 03:11.941
MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

03:12.025 --> 03:15.612
Ughh! This exam is covering way too much
material!

03:15.695 --> 03:17.697
Well, why didn't you start studying
earlier?

03:17.780 --> 03:18.781
So Minato...

03:19.282 --> 03:20.783
Why'd you leave and come back?

03:20.867 --> 03:22.118
I forgot my notebook.

03:22.660 --> 03:23.912
And I needed it to study.

03:24.537 --> 03:25.788
I don't get any of it!

03:25.872 --> 03:26.831
Oh, come on.

03:27.790 --> 03:29.459
The four of us studying together.

03:30.710 --> 03:34.088
This all feels... So foreign to me.

03:35.465 --> 03:37.091
Oh. Have you heard, Miki?

03:37.175 --> 03:39.010
- Mm?
- Yeah, I got dumped again.

03:39.093 --> 03:40.803
I'm sorry, what?! When was this?

03:40.887 --> 03:43.264
- Two days ago.
- Wait, this just happened?

03:43.765 --> 03:45.350
Why? What'd you do wrong?

03:45.433 --> 03:47.227
Why do you assume it's my fault?

03:47.727 --> 03:50.772
- Wow, okay I see how it is. Automatically
- Oh, please, it's pretty much always

03:50.855 --> 03:52.398
- your fault. Did you say something dumb
- assume Minato's the jerk. Thanks guys.

03:52.482 --> 03:56.361
- Your fault. Did you say something dumb
- Assume Minato's the jerk. Thanks guys.

03:56.444 --> 03:58.571
Man... I'm never the one doing the dumping.

03:59.072 --> 04:00.657
That's what bothers you?

04:02.492 --> 04:03.618
- What? Surprised?
- No.

04:03.701 --> 04:04.535
No I'm...

04:06.496 --> 04:07.747
How do I put this?

04:11.209 --> 04:13.336
I thought when someone got dumped they'd
be...

04:13.419 --> 04:14.504
Well, a bit more...

04:16.673 --> 04:22.595
I dunno, maybe depressed or bitter, like,
holding a grudge or something?

04:24.430 --> 04:25.265
But why?

04:27.100 --> 04:32.105
For me, I just appreciate someone was
into me, even for a short time.

04:32.188 --> 04:33.314
You know what I mean?

04:33.398 --> 04:35.191
- Like "Thank you!"
- Yeah, right.

04:35.275 --> 04:36.526
- Hah!
- Hm?

04:38.152 --> 04:40.989
How can someone be so casual about a
breakup?

04:41.864 --> 04:43.866
Oh. Was I too casual about it?

04:43.950 --> 04:44.784
Agh!

04:45.743 --> 04:48.288
I don't show it, but I'm definitely
still hurt by it.

04:48.371 --> 04:49.372
So...

04:50.456 --> 04:51.291
Oh no...

04:51.958 --> 04:54.294
I should've been more sensitive about it.

04:55.044 --> 04:55.878
DOWN

04:55.962 --> 04:58.047
I-I, um... I'm sorry.

05:00.216 --> 05:01.259
I forgive ya.

05:02.051 --> 05:03.553
Can I cry on your shoulder?

05:06.097 --> 05:06.931
Uh.

05:09.475 --> 05:11.644
Yeah, no, that'll be enough of
that, thanks!

05:11.728 --> 05:14.105
Oh, Minato, you're such a kidder, you.

05:14.188 --> 05:15.606
You're crushing... my face.

05:16.107 --> 05:17.066
Koyun...

05:17.150 --> 05:20.403
Minato's always messing around,
so you can just ignore him.

05:20.486 --> 05:21.529
Oh.

05:21.612 --> 05:22.655
What does that mean?

05:22.739 --> 05:23.740
Mm.

05:25.074 --> 05:26.784
Hm? Miki?

05:27.869 --> 05:30.330
- Hey, Yota-sensei, I don't get this part.
- Mm?

05:30.413 --> 05:31.372
Hm?

05:31.456 --> 05:32.332
Ah!

05:32.415 --> 05:33.249
Oh, my gosh!

05:33.333 --> 05:35.335
Ah, ha, oh no, I did it again! Oh man.
I'm so sorry!

05:35.418 --> 05:37.462
Jeez! Are you kidding me? There you
go again with your clumsy self.

05:37.545 --> 05:38.379
I- I'm clumsy?

05:38.921 --> 05:41.466
Yeah! You're always dropping things.
That's literally the definition

05:41.549 --> 05:43.217
- Yeah, yeah.
- of clumsy.

05:43.301 --> 05:44.469
Let me... Well... Oh, crap.

05:45.636 --> 05:47.722
FLUSTER
JEEZ!

05:48.222 --> 05:50.099
Here. Is that everything?

05:50.183 --> 05:51.351
Whew, thanks.

05:57.023 --> 05:59.567
She laughs, so she's human after all.

06:02.570 --> 06:03.404
Oh.

06:05.656 --> 06:06.491
Okay.

06:06.574 --> 06:08.284
Me and Koyun are going this way.

06:08.368 --> 06:09.619
Should I walk you there?

06:09.702 --> 06:12.121
No, you don't have to, but thanks
for offering.

06:12.205 --> 06:15.124
Yeah, I dare someone to mess with us
while I'm here. I've got killer grip

06:15.208 --> 06:16.042
strength!

06:16.125 --> 06:17.627
Yeah, she's not messing around.

06:17.710 --> 06:19.420
You be careful too, Miki.

06:21.923 --> 06:24.425
See ya, Yota! Thanks so much for
your help today!

06:24.509 --> 06:25.676
Hey, what about me?

06:25.760 --> 06:27.303
I helped you with English.

06:27.387 --> 06:28.471
Oh yeah, you too.

06:28.554 --> 06:29.514
Gee, thanks a lot.

06:30.014 --> 06:33.976
Koyun, I'm dying to eat at Da Pote
across from the station. Can we stop by?

06:34.060 --> 06:36.062
Sure, but what happened to dinner at
home?

06:36.145 --> 06:38.731
Don't worry, I'll have room. This is an
appetizer.

06:39.649 --> 06:40.483
Ridiculous.

06:40.566 --> 06:42.610
It's true! I've got a separate
stomach for it!

06:42.693 --> 06:44.404
Miki sure does talk a lot, huh?

06:44.904 --> 06:46.781
She should be like that all the time.

06:47.907 --> 06:49.325
So, what're you doin' now?

06:49.409 --> 06:50.326
Hm?

06:50.410 --> 06:51.619
WIENER DOG EXTRA FILLING

06:51.702 --> 06:55.164
I'm having one of these bad boys!
On the way to the community center.

06:55.248 --> 06:56.082
Are you serious?

06:56.165 --> 06:58.543
You're gonna give yourself food
poisoning, man!

06:59.335 --> 07:00.795
Wanna have dinner at my place?

07:00.878 --> 07:02.880
Mom loves it whenever you come over.

07:02.964 --> 07:03.881
Mmmm.

07:03.965 --> 07:05.675
Nah, I gotta go study some more.

07:06.175 --> 07:07.844
- See ya.
- Okay.

07:09.679 --> 07:11.389
You're making me look bad, ya know.

07:11.472 --> 07:12.807
Nah, that's impossible.

07:14.600 --> 07:16.144
In more ways than one.

07:18.146 --> 07:18.980
Hm.

07:21.691 --> 07:23.067
Yota was acting like that, but...

07:23.151 --> 07:24.569
WASH YOUR HANDS AND GARGLE

07:24.652 --> 07:25.570
What about her?

07:27.071 --> 07:28.489
I wonder how she feels.

07:31.200 --> 07:34.954
Could it be that maybe she's into him?

07:36.414 --> 07:37.248
Hmmm.

07:39.584 --> 07:42.044
I don't think Yota would be a good fit
for her.

07:48.509 --> 07:50.011
- Hey, wait for me!
- So, Koyun...

07:54.307 --> 07:56.017
Huh? I only met him recently.

07:56.517 --> 07:59.395
Like, literally the day before we walked
home together.

08:01.022 --> 08:03.649
He just came up to talk to me randomly in
the stairwell.

08:03.733 --> 08:05.735
- What'd he say?
- Hm?

08:08.613 --> 08:09.447
Uh.

08:10.990 --> 08:11.824
Uh...

08:13.659 --> 08:14.994
Wait... What did he say?

08:15.495 --> 08:16.496
Argh!

08:17.288 --> 08:20.374
We didn't really talk about anything
important, to be honest.

08:21.250 --> 08:22.627
Sorry to disappoint.

08:22.710 --> 08:23.836
Oh, Koyun...

08:23.920 --> 08:25.755
That's so like you.

08:28.466 --> 08:29.592
Well, alright.

08:29.675 --> 08:31.052
I guess it's fine, then.

08:31.135 --> 08:31.969
No worries.

08:33.596 --> 08:34.847
Wait, does Miki...

08:44.941 --> 08:46.192
Could she possibly...

08:54.492 --> 08:56.285
I wish I hadn't overslept.

08:58.287 --> 09:01.999
I prefer walking to school before
everyone else, to avoid the crowds.

09:03.876 --> 09:06.546
Yeah, I should've left, like, thirty
minutes earlier.

09:09.632 --> 09:11.259
During exams...

09:11.968 --> 09:16.305
In the mornings, the usually packed
streets are so quiet.

09:25.731 --> 09:27.775
I prefer it, for some reason.

09:30.945 --> 09:33.072
You normally come to school round
this time?

09:33.155 --> 09:34.156
Huh?

09:34.240 --> 09:35.074
Morning.

09:35.866 --> 09:39.036
When I saw you, I was worried I came to
school too early today.

09:39.120 --> 09:40.204
Miss Earlybird.

09:40.746 --> 09:41.581
Well...

09:42.248 --> 09:43.082
Uh, I...

09:44.083 --> 09:46.919
I normally come much later during
non-exam times.

09:47.003 --> 09:50.131
Today, I was originally hoping to
come even earlier, but then...

09:50.923 --> 09:52.383
That's too much explanation.

09:53.759 --> 09:54.802
No, I usually...

09:55.595 --> 09:56.429
Don't.

09:57.847 --> 10:01.350
SILENCE

10:02.268 --> 10:03.311
Okay, think...

10:03.394 --> 10:06.564
- Snacks, weather, Yota, studying, Miki,
- SCHOOL EVENTS, SNACKS, WEATHER, YOTA

10:06.647 --> 10:07.481
- TV...
- CURRENT EVENTS, MIKI, STUDYING, CLASS 2

10:07.565 --> 10:09.400
STUDENTS, TV JR. HIGH SCHOOL

10:09.483 --> 10:10.735
I've been meaning to ask.

10:11.527 --> 10:13.613
Igarashi... You know him?

10:15.281 --> 10:17.116
Hm? Wait.

10:17.617 --> 10:19.952
Wh- What did he just ask me?

10:22.038 --> 10:22.872
Igarashi?

10:24.415 --> 10:26.083
Oh, why? Do you know him?

10:26.584 --> 10:30.338
Well, our soccer team has joint practices
with West High School sometimes.

10:30.838 --> 10:32.048
That's where I met him.

10:33.174 --> 10:35.051
Just wondering if you two were friends.

10:35.134 --> 10:37.136
Would he know you if I brought you up?

10:37.219 --> 10:39.096
No. We had no connection at all.

10:39.180 --> 10:40.264
I- I didn't know him.

10:41.182 --> 10:42.850
I doubt he'd recognize my name.

10:43.934 --> 10:44.769
Ah, gotcha.

10:44.852 --> 10:48.689
Well, he's visiting our school soon,
but you don't know each other, so never

10:48.773 --> 10:50.024
- mind.
- When?

10:50.107 --> 10:52.234
For a scrimmage, on the last day of
exams.

10:52.985 --> 10:53.819
Oh, okay.

10:54.528 --> 10:55.988
Definitely going home early.

10:59.617 --> 11:00.451
I wonder...

11:01.202 --> 11:04.622
Does the fact he's asking about him mean
that Amamiya is buddy-buddy

11:04.705 --> 11:06.415
with Igarashi?

11:06.916 --> 11:09.418
Yeah, our soccer team and his
school's team are planning to have a

11:09.502 --> 11:11.420
joint practice on the last day of exams.

11:11.504 --> 11:14.507
At the very least they're close enough to
know which schools the other went to.

11:14.590 --> 11:15.424
I'm pretty excited. I think it'll be fun,

11:15.508 --> 11:16.342
I can't focus on anything he's saying.

11:16.425 --> 11:18.844
And we'll totally kick their butts...

11:33.401 --> 11:34.360
Oh, and by the way!

11:34.902 --> 11:37.071
I brought last year's final exam
questions.

11:37.655 --> 11:40.783
I heard each year the questions
tend to be pretty much the same.

11:40.866 --> 11:42.910
Huh? How'd you get something like that?

11:42.993 --> 11:45.454
Well, I may've asked a senior for
a little favor.

11:47.164 --> 11:49.667
You coming to our classroom after school
today?

11:49.750 --> 11:50.876
Uh.

11:50.960 --> 11:51.794
Mm-hm.

11:52.920 --> 11:54.088
Awesome, see you then.

11:54.839 --> 11:55.881
BOW

12:00.761 --> 12:02.680
Morning. How's it goin'?

12:04.390 --> 12:06.016
What's the best way to put this?

12:07.518 --> 12:08.978
He can talk to anybody. He's like

12:09.061 --> 12:11.772
- some kinda, I dunno... communication
- SEEMS LIKE A COMMUNICATION EXPERT...

12:11.856 --> 12:13.190
- expert.
- Oh boy...

12:16.193 --> 12:18.237
I wonder how Miki feels about Amamiya?

12:19.363 --> 12:22.283
I mean, I don't really have proof of
anything just yet.

12:23.617 --> 12:26.871
But Miki was clearly very concerned
about how me and Amamiya knew

12:26.954 --> 12:27.788
each other.

12:30.040 --> 12:32.168
And him knowing Igarashi worries me.

12:33.210 --> 12:36.297
I think it might be best if I just keep
my distance from him.

12:42.887 --> 12:45.306
All I want is some peace and quiet.

12:51.729 --> 12:53.397
Koyun and Minato.

12:58.319 --> 13:00.404
- This is Yota.
- He's giant!

13:01.864 --> 13:04.074
And my little brother is like, super
strong.

13:04.784 --> 13:06.994
Mm-hm.
Yeah, we stopped by on the way home.

13:07.077 --> 13:08.078
The usual store.

13:09.079 --> 13:10.623
What're you worried about?

13:10.706 --> 13:12.541
I wonder what sides I got for lunch.

13:12.625 --> 13:13.751
Yeah, I can't wait.

13:13.834 --> 13:15.795
Oh. Er, Miki, do you wanna trade sides?

13:16.295 --> 13:17.797
Yeah, sure! I'm game!

13:19.006 --> 13:20.424
TUES 2ND, GRADE MEETING THURS 4TH,

13:20.508 --> 13:23.219
- THIRD PTA MEETING MON 8TH, GYM CLEANING
- Look, Hikawa.

13:23.302 --> 13:26.138
I appreciate your diligence and all, but
why don't you go out and enjoy your

13:26.222 --> 13:27.056
lunch break?

13:27.598 --> 13:29.433
The teacher's lounge is warmer.

13:29.517 --> 13:31.143
Are you a cat or something?

13:31.936 --> 13:33.479
Anyway, where were we?

13:33.979 --> 13:34.814
Oh right.

13:34.897 --> 13:37.525
You do it like this, then like this, and
there you go.

13:37.608 --> 13:39.151
Oh, I see now.

13:39.902 --> 13:42.321
Well good, I'm glad you understand,
now go have fun.

13:42.404 --> 13:45.074
- Shoo!
- Hmph. I'm going to Noriko's office.

13:45.616 --> 13:47.284
Don't just chase heaters all day.

13:49.370 --> 13:50.996
She certainly comes here often.

13:51.080 --> 13:52.706
Yeah, she really does.

13:53.457 --> 13:56.627
You know, I don't think I've
ever seen her hanging out with any

13:56.710 --> 13:58.337
other students. That worries me.

14:00.965 --> 14:04.051
Maybe she just feels more comfortable
being around grown ups.

14:04.635 --> 14:08.347
Cause you see, well, teachers have
to keep a certain professional distance

14:08.430 --> 14:10.307
between them and their students.

14:10.391 --> 14:13.811
There's a sense of security in
knowing that teachers are, in a sense,

14:13.894 --> 14:16.105
strangers who don't pry or get too
personal.

14:16.772 --> 14:17.606
Whatever!

14:21.110 --> 14:22.027
- But Ms. Suwa...
- Lounge.

14:22.111 --> 14:25.197
Sometimes you have to let people
live their own live and not shove your

14:25.281 --> 14:26.824
values down their throats.

14:26.907 --> 14:29.994
Matsumoto, what on earth happened to
you, huh?

14:31.370 --> 14:32.329
Let's see.

14:32.997 --> 14:36.250
Okay, I need my paint set and my
sketchbook.

14:37.334 --> 14:39.086
Do I need anything else for class?

14:39.169 --> 14:40.379
Or is that it?

14:42.172 --> 14:43.007
Hm?

14:43.591 --> 14:44.758
PEEK

14:44.842 --> 14:47.052
- Wait, are you being serious or are you
- Oh, it's Amamiya.

14:47.136 --> 14:47.970
Messing with me?

14:48.053 --> 14:49.471
- A MEMORY COMING BACK
- Why'd you ignore me?

14:49.555 --> 14:50.639
Flashback. My bubble.

14:52.600 --> 14:53.434
Well...

14:53.517 --> 14:55.895
He's surrounded by a bunch of
guys I don't know.

14:55.978 --> 14:58.355
Good. He hasn't even noticed I'm here.

14:58.439 --> 15:00.274
Be stealthy, like a panther.

15:00.900 --> 15:03.777
Mm. Technically, this isn't ignoring him.

15:05.070 --> 15:08.991
I- I just need to avoid being spotted and
make my escape.

15:10.117 --> 15:12.870
Oh, no, no, no, he's looking right at me!

15:12.953 --> 15:16.165
- Now give 'em the old quick bow and slip
- THE "QUICK BOW AND SLIP AWAY" TACTIC

15:16.248 --> 15:17.082
away tactic.

15:17.166 --> 15:18.000
YAY!

15:18.083 --> 15:19.668
- Oh no, he's drawing more attention.
- Hm?

15:19.752 --> 15:20.669
- Hm?
- Hm?

15:20.753 --> 15:22.338
- What is it? What's up?
- Stare.

15:23.047 --> 15:24.715
- Stare.
- Stare.

15:24.798 --> 15:26.508
- Stare.
- GAZE, GAZE, GAZE, GAZE

15:26.592 --> 15:28.969
Stop, stop! Just ignore me. Pretend
I'm not here or something.

15:29.053 --> 15:30.054
- Hm?
- One sec, guys.

15:30.137 --> 15:30.971
Poof!

15:31.055 --> 15:31.889
Poof!

15:32.890 --> 15:35.559
- Poof!
- Huh? W-w-why would he do that?

15:35.643 --> 15:36.477
Poof!

15:36.560 --> 15:39.229
- He's coming this way.
- Why are you hiding over here?

15:40.230 --> 15:42.483
Silly, you could've just said hi,
know you.

15:42.566 --> 15:44.026
Instead of just lurking.

15:44.693 --> 15:45.778
Oh. Yeah, I...

15:45.861 --> 15:47.446
Well, while I'm here...

15:48.489 --> 15:51.200
- Let me get your phone number.
- Distance...

15:58.874 --> 16:01.085
- Awesome, thank you.
- Mmm.

16:02.920 --> 16:04.046
What's in the bag?

16:05.255 --> 16:07.341
I have art class next, so it's uh...

16:08.217 --> 16:10.052
- Stuff for that.
- Oh, right.

16:10.761 --> 16:12.554
Class 2 has art as an elective.

16:12.638 --> 16:13.889
So, what do you do?

16:13.973 --> 16:14.974
You oil painting?

16:16.308 --> 16:19.228
No, we're... working with acrylic
right now.

16:19.812 --> 16:20.771
We're gonna crush it!

16:20.854 --> 16:21.897
Sure.

16:25.150 --> 16:25.985
Miki.

16:28.904 --> 16:30.239
- Oops.
- What's up?

16:30.322 --> 16:31.240
Huh? Uh, sorry!

16:31.323 --> 16:32.866
I better get going.

16:32.950 --> 16:34.743
- Run away!
- Oh...

16:37.287 --> 16:38.998
She was all by herself again.

16:41.208 --> 16:44.378
- TOWARD YOTA SMILE, HEE-HEE-HEE, RELIEVED
- Yota.

16:45.212 --> 16:47.006
- TOWARD MINATO NEW
- Gotta stop by my locker.

16:47.089 --> 16:48.632
Yeah, I better get going.

16:49.675 --> 16:50.509
Man...

16:50.592 --> 16:54.555
She acts so differently towards
someone she likes than to everyone else.

16:54.638 --> 16:57.641
- "Everyone else" means...
- EVERYONE ELSE->

17:00.853 --> 17:01.687
Yo, dude.

17:01.770 --> 17:04.648
I can't believe you had the guts
to talk to the Ice Queen.

17:04.732 --> 17:07.359
- I swear, you must have nerves of steel.
- Yeah. Well...

17:07.443 --> 17:09.737
I was hoping to get a bit closer to
her, but...

17:09.820 --> 17:11.113
Guess I scared her off.

17:13.073 --> 17:14.199
Kinda sad, right?

17:14.283 --> 17:15.200
Please, Minato.

17:15.284 --> 17:17.077
What would you know about sadness?

17:17.161 --> 17:18.120
Ha, right?

17:18.203 --> 17:20.664
What? Come on, I'm not like a robot or
something.

17:28.714 --> 17:30.299
Questions from last years exam!

17:30.883 --> 17:31.759
Minato...

17:32.509 --> 17:33.343
You're the best!

17:33.927 --> 17:36.430
Once I memorize these, it'll be a piece
of cake.

17:36.513 --> 17:38.640
Don't let your guard down now, Miki.

17:38.724 --> 17:39.808
Stay sharp.

17:40.309 --> 17:43.562
I heard the average score on the
last math exam was really low...

17:44.063 --> 17:46.273
So maybe they'll make this next
one easier.

17:46.356 --> 17:47.941
Man, I sure hope so!

17:48.442 --> 17:51.695
What'd you score on that test where
everyone did terribly, Yota?

17:51.779 --> 17:52.780
Hmm.

17:52.863 --> 17:53.781
Oh, come on!

17:54.698 --> 17:55.532
I'm confused.

17:55.616 --> 17:58.243
Because you could've tested into
East High School.

17:58.327 --> 18:00.204
And they have a basketball team.

18:00.287 --> 18:01.455
So why'd you come here?

18:01.538 --> 18:02.414
Huh?

18:02.498 --> 18:04.416
Oh, it's just closer to my house.

18:04.500 --> 18:07.002
You were okay with settling cause it
was closer?

18:07.086 --> 18:08.087
That's not why.

18:08.170 --> 18:12.091
He chose a less challenging school so
he'd be top of his class and get into

18:12.174 --> 18:13.008
a better college.

18:13.092 --> 18:16.428
He won't admit it, cause he knows you
barely made it in here, Miki.

18:16.512 --> 18:17.346
Wait. Is that true?

18:17.429 --> 18:18.972
Whoa! Hey, come on, Minato.

18:19.056 --> 18:20.516
That's not what it is.

18:20.599 --> 18:22.476
We live in very different worlds.

18:22.559 --> 18:23.977
Oh, stop, Miki...

18:26.230 --> 18:27.064
Mm?

18:27.147 --> 18:29.650
Koyun, wow, you're awfully focused today.

18:29.733 --> 18:31.568
- Hm?
- Oh, he changed the subject!

18:32.069 --> 18:35.823
Well, I was trying to be zen and clear
my mind of distractions.

18:36.657 --> 18:39.076
Wait, you're saying you have
distractions?

18:39.159 --> 18:39.993
Yeah.

18:40.077 --> 18:41.537
- NG
- My mind is full of them.

18:45.207 --> 18:47.626
Hm. She does act differently.

18:48.544 --> 18:49.837
Tell me, Hikawa

18:51.130 --> 18:51.964
You single?

18:54.466 --> 18:55.300
Huh?

18:56.552 --> 18:57.386
Oh, well...

18:58.053 --> 18:58.887
Uh, yeah.

19:00.180 --> 19:01.431
Why is he asking me that?

19:02.558 --> 19:04.017
Oh. I see.

19:05.310 --> 19:06.186
What was that?

19:06.687 --> 19:08.856
I wonder why he's asking me that.

19:09.815 --> 19:11.358
Igarashi... You know him?

19:14.153 --> 19:17.865
Could it be that Igarashi maybe put
him up to this?

19:18.615 --> 19:20.701
No way. I- I'm reading too much into it.

19:21.243 --> 19:22.870
He wouldn't send a spy.

19:23.495 --> 19:24.913
It was a long time ago.

19:24.997 --> 19:26.498
Even he wouldn't go that far.

19:27.207 --> 19:28.083
Minato.

19:29.334 --> 19:31.420
I wouldn't advise going after Koyun.

19:36.133 --> 19:37.801
Wait, is that's why he asked?

19:38.844 --> 19:40.179
Sorry, Dad, I can't do that?

19:40.262 --> 19:41.638
You can't have her hand.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.724
Ahh, he was just joking.

19:45.851 --> 19:47.436
I guess I was overthinking it.

19:48.270 --> 19:50.772
I'm so neurotic and paranoid too.

19:51.440 --> 19:52.274
Embarrassing.

19:54.151 --> 19:54.985
Oh no! Miki!

19:56.653 --> 19:57.779
Uhh. Agh!

19:59.072 --> 20:00.365
I can't read her face.

20:00.449 --> 20:01.575
What do I do now?

20:02.117 --> 20:05.579
She's my childhood best friend,
yet I can't tell what she's thinking.

20:06.997 --> 20:10.167
So, anyway...
I'm gonna hunt down some sugar!

20:10.792 --> 20:12.461
- SUGAR
- Sugar?

20:12.544 --> 20:13.378
Huh?

20:13.462 --> 20:14.963
Heading to the vending machine.

20:15.047 --> 20:17.341
Koyun and Yota, I'll buy you
something too.

20:17.424 --> 20:20.010
- What about me?
- Buy your own stuff, Minato.

20:20.093 --> 20:21.094
Hey.

20:22.221 --> 20:24.306
Or... Just come along.

20:30.145 --> 20:31.939
Ugh. I guess I could.

20:37.027 --> 20:38.195
We'll be right back!

20:45.285 --> 20:46.119
Miki?

20:47.913 --> 20:52.000
Okay, Miki.
Care to explain what that was all about?

20:55.337 --> 20:56.964
RIGHT BEFORE THE ACTUAL EXAM! PASS THE
EXAM

20:57.047 --> 20:58.715
The manga you recommended was great,
Ishida!

20:58.799 --> 21:00.884
Alright then, see you later, Yoshino!

21:01.385 --> 21:02.302
Hey, Yamashita!

21:02.803 --> 21:05.389
That anime you were telling me about the
other day?

21:05.472 --> 21:08.600
- Well, I finally got around to watching it
- Is it just me, or is Minato basically

21:08.684 --> 21:11.144
- and, man! I basically binge-watched
- always talking to someone?

21:11.228 --> 21:13.230
- The entire thing. It was so good. What
- Really? Huh.

21:13.313 --> 21:14.398
He's like that at school too.

21:14.481 --> 21:16.191
- Should I check out next?
- That's nice.

21:16.275 --> 21:17.901
I wish I could be like that.

21:17.985 --> 21:19.319
Minato collects strays.

21:19.820 --> 21:23.699
It's like, if he sees a loner, he refuses
to let them stay that way for long.

21:24.491 --> 21:27.327
- Huh?
- Yeah, it's cause he feels sorry for them.

21:29.496 --> 21:31.290
He feels sorry for them?

21:37.921 --> 21:38.755
Wait.

21:39.589 --> 21:42.009
This one's on me.
I need to buy one for Hikawa.

21:46.471 --> 21:47.306
But why?

21:47.973 --> 21:51.893
The other day, I snuck up on her and she
jumped...

21:51.977 --> 21:55.439
Which made her hit the button and
buy a weird flavor.

21:56.106 --> 21:59.443
Oh, it was this one.
Funny, I only just remembered that.

22:06.283 --> 22:07.409
Hey, Minato...

22:12.164 --> 22:14.458
Be honest, do you like Koyun?

22:22.132 --> 22:22.966
Huh?
